diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..e53f6af 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -159,3 +159,65 @@ __Response:__
 ```
 
 `request` and `response` can be `null` for deliveries that have not started yet or are still in progress. The delivery request headers omit the `X-Webhook-Signature` header.
+
+## Deliveries
+
+Whenever something happens on the board that a webhook is subscribed to, Fizzy makes a single `POST` to the webhook's payload URL. Each event is delivered exactly once per webhook: there are no retries, and the delivery log shows how each attempt went.
+
+__Request headers:__
+
+| Header | Value |
+|--------|-------|
+| `Content-Type` | `application/json` (or `text/html` for Campfire) |
+| `User-Agent` | `fizzy/1.0.0 Webhook` |
+| `X-Webhook-Signature` | Hex-encoded `HMAC-SHA256` of the raw request body, keyed with the webhook's `signing_secret` |
+| `X-Webhook-Timestamp` | When the event happened, in ISO 8601 |
+
+Verify a delivery by computing the HMAC of the body you received and comparing it with the signature header:
+
+```ruby
+OpenSSL::HMAC.hexdigest("SHA256", signing_secret, request.raw_post) == request.headers["X-Webhook-Signature"]
+```
+
+__Request body:__
+
+```json
+{
+  "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohde",
+  "action": "card_closed",
+  "created_at": "2025-12-05T19:36:35.401Z",
+  "particulars": {},
+  "eventable": {
+    "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohdb",
+    "number": 42,
+    "title": "Fix mobile login",
+    "status": "closed",
+    "url": "http://app.fizzy.localhost:3006/897362094/cards/42",
+    "...": "the same card (or comment) representation as the rest of the API"
+  },
+  "board": { "id": "03f5v9zkft4hj9qq0lsn9ohcy", "name": "Fizzy", "...": "…" },
+  "creator": { "id": "03f5v9zjw7pz8717a4no1h8a7", "name": "David Heinemeier Hansson", "...": "…" }
+}
+```
+
+`eventable` is a card for every `card_*` action and a comment for `comment_created`. `particulars` follows the same shape as in [Activities](activities.md).
+
+Webhooks pointing at chat services get a message instead of the event JSON, so they can be used without any code in between:
+
+- __Slack__ incoming webhooks (`https://hooks.slack.com/services/…`) receive `{ "text": "David added \"Fix mobile login\" <https://…|↗︎>" }`.
+- __Campfire__ bot URLs (`…/rooms/:room_id/:bot_key/messages`) receive the message as HTML.
+- __Basecamp__ chatbot URLs (`…/integrations/:key/buckets/:bucket_id/chats/:chat_id/lines`) receive `{ "content": "<html message>" }`.
+
+__Responses:__
+
+A delivery succeeds when the receiver answers with a `2xx` status. Any other status, or not getting a response at all, counts as a failure. Redirects are not followed. Requests time out after 5 seconds when connecting and 10 seconds when waiting for a response, and the payload URL must resolve to a public IP address — receivers on private or loopback networks are unreachable.
+
+Each delivery in the log has a `state` of `pending`, `in_progress`, `completed` (a response was received, its status code is in `response.code`), or `errored` (no response; `response.error` says why: `destination_unreachable`, `timeout`, `ssl_error`, or `connection_failed`).
+
+__Switching off failing receivers:__
+
+A webhook that keeps failing is switched off: after 10 failed deliveries in a row spanning at least an hour, it's deactivated (`"active": false`) and stops receiving events. A single successful delivery resets the count. Once the receiver is fixed, reactivate the webhook with `POST /:account_slug/boards/:board_id/webhooks/:id/activation`; that also resets the failure count.
+
+__Retention:__
+
+Deliveries are kept for a week, after which they're removed from the log.
